v 2.1.0
d 'SJCLEAN': Stata module to rejoin and re-break log files for LaTeX inclusion
d 
d sjclean tidies a Stata log that is about to be typeset. Stata breaks a log
d line at c(linesize) and marks the continuation with ">", an artifact of a
d terminal width chosen before anybody knew what column the line would be
d printed in. sjclean rejoins the logical line and re-breaks it at a width
d you state, with the continuation shown as an indent, as Stata's marker, or
d not at all.
d 
d Machine paths are anonymised by default: the directory part of every
d absolute path is replaced by <path>/ and only the filename is kept, so a
d published log does not disclose a username, a machine layout or the
d topology of an internal network. Relative paths, which are safe and
d informative, are untouched. noanonymize turns this off.
d 
d The right width is a property of the target environment and is measurable:
d the shipped probes report 96 characters for stlog[beamer] and 80 for stlog
d in the Stata Journal class.
d 
d KW: logs
d KW: LaTeX
d KW: Stata Journal
d KW: sjlatex
d KW: reproducible research
d 
d Requires: Stata version 14
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20260813
d 
d Author: Joao Pedro Azevedo, UNICEF
d Support: email jpazevedo@unicef.org
d 
